{"title":"2023 APMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_APMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/6544a738902cf91c957b57767738b8fbdb379516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{p(n)-1}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"45\" />, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb912f901cc0dba33ac9d06a90b262b423d9eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the sum of all positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the largest prime divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_APMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Answer: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Rearrange the equation to the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1f44a4565c141de4933e07ff0e9c3eec92bd455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)-1=\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"40\" />, then do case work on the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> grows large, we can see that the right hand side becomes always smaller than the left hand side. We can use the geometric series sum fomula to show this inequality.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>For example, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c24cfe74427f691654e69a57eab5890004546a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a65319f55f5feb23d64bd2bb45f22adfb73016ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2^a3^b5^c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7503da2925135f18eff73ba9bd2ca75151cf76a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)-1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2ffda9e21969f36b6491e18f7ad0a99b1d48ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{n}=\\frac{\\sigma(2^a)}{2^a}\\frac{\\sigma(3^b)}{3^b}\\frac{\\sigma(5^c)}{5^c}\\leq2\\times{\\frac{3}{2}}\\times{\\frac{5}{4}}=3.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"363\" height=\"41\" />. The left hand side is always greater.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea4e0d74a71e6b728ad824d333f3f13b3cf84c32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/87948df1b13738a3532321e392881ddc8b058540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2^a3^b5^c7^d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d94f4b39843764b0f36237ca0a4c0369cd314d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)-1=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd26fccb13bab84b4780aebfeb4a8ccc58c72a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{n}=\\frac{\\sigma(2^a)}{2^a}\\frac{\\sigma(3^b)}{3^b}\\frac{\\sigma(5^c)}{5^c}\\frac{\\sigma(7^d)}{7^d}\\leq2\\times{\\frac{3}{2}}\\times{\\frac{5}{4}}\\times{\\frac{7}{6}}=4.375$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"453\" height=\"41\" />. The left hand side is always greater.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>In general, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4cc44dfa9d27eb68b8011024b1ed059d786702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)\\geq{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d716539d909af43977f3c14cc6afa2fbd215b608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{n}=\\frac{\\sigma(2^a)}{2^a}\\frac{\\sigma(3^b)}{3^b}\\frac{\\sigma(5^c)}{5^c}\\frac{\\sigma(7^d)}{7^d}......$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"279\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b712d6689cf489277810f759a6c30d5015ba3ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq2\\times{\\frac{3}{2}}\\times{\\frac{5}{4}}\\times{\\frac{7}{6}}\\times{......}\\times{\\frac{p(n)}{p(n)-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"280\" height=\"45\" />   Notice that this product can telescope if some more fractions are multiplied.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7c0599544b4183a22177241eebdc6449ba22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq2\\times{\\frac{3}{2}}\\times{\\frac{4}{3}}\\times{\\frac{5}{4}}\\times{\\frac{6}{5}}\\times{\\frac{7}{6}}\\times{......}\\times{\\frac{p(n)}{p(n)-1}}\\div{{\\frac{4}{3}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"386\" height=\"45\" /> Such a very loose bound is enough.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/777d14af6e1ead4c9eaee26f8fda531c58f0a27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq p(n)\\div{{\\frac{4}{3}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>We now have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428f6bd44f599754dcd4ff205eac7259a8a70a76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)-1\\leq p(n)\\div{{\\frac{4}{3}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3ac3430424bf7746616ec2d47b50494ab4ab04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p(n)}{4}\\leq{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"40\" />. This is impossible for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4cc44dfa9d27eb68b8011024b1ed059d786702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)\\geq{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>As a result, we only need to consider the cases of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad68495b627cc6a20e8b6003cdbbd942460f0a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c9975f4e1331806417f8ffcc6de21daf15e6e9cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>The case of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad68495b627cc6a20e8b6003cdbbd942460f0a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" /> is simple. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea76ac66db576b64a83e7e512af7419c41902364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)-1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb912f901cc0dba33ac9d06a90b262b423d9eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> includes both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> itself. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7b39861384ea84ab3f3daeaf7057c7dbb2ae86e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{n}\\geq \\frac{1}{n}+\\frac{n}{n} &gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"40\" />. The right hand side is always greater.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c9975f4e1331806417f8ffcc6de21daf15e6e9cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44ecb313f68a7ecb2f594b331e5b32a3867b5714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2^a3^b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31eecdda266744450ebcbef2e7b1c8e323440482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)-1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b00ef3daea0d34ec858b11746d12d30ab994aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sigma(n)}{n}=\\frac{\\sigma(2^a)}{2^a}\\frac{\\sigma(3^b)}{3^b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784c772cd852198dc8b0fd74f0fa757448615176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{2})^{a+1}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{3})^{b+1}}{1-\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"189\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>First prove that having both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a86dc7d6f6223a287b2870c0be46d999b0fc9ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd5ebb5bb41851d9c2ddf6ee9e0460f359fbec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> makes the right hand side greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. When we have both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a86dc7d6f6223a287b2870c0be46d999b0fc9ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd5ebb5bb41851d9c2ddf6ee9e0460f359fbec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, the right hand side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f21718b3257a60e10eb7c75a3dec2bdf1f396782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\geq \\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{2})^{3}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{3})^{3}}{1-\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{91}{36}&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"236\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>Than list the cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />. After solving the eqautions\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e27ae05aa3ec85999b4efc238c9b144c260b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2=\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{3})^{b+1}}{1-\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"119\" height=\"49\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a52afd9548eeb23494efac3d0e300129ce23ddbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2=\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{2})^{2}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{3})^{b+1}}{1-\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"186\" height=\"49\" />, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8613c054962a203b5476aecce4e5ec43aa9c4d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2=\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{2})^{a+1}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{3})^{2}}{1-\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"188\" height=\"49\" />,\n</p><p>we will discover that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> is the only solution to the equation.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>The only answer to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1cb6de708e665d67b330c86d7a64c2d384a52f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2\\times{3}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" />. The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> does satisfy the equation can be checked easily.\n</p><p><br />\n~G2JFForever\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_APMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xkIm0k1FE-8\">https://youtu.be/xkIm0k1FE-8</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018023416\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 288/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11095/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25076:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018023416 and revision id 281409. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}